  "title": "Joseon dynasty",
  "summary": "The Joseon dynasty ruled Korea from 1392, when general Yi Seong-gye overthrew the Goryeo dynasty and, as King Taejo, moved the capital to Hanyang, modern Seoul. Sejong the Great (r. 1418–1450) personally created the Korean alphabet, Hangul. Neo-Confucianism and other lasting Korean traditions can be traced to this era, which saw long periods of peace broken by invasions from Japan and China.",
